The query in `1result.sql` is the safest choice:

• It uses the 5‑year age–group table, which is already aggregated (faster than summing all single‑year & sex rows).  
• It explicitly restricts to `total_flag = 'A'` and `age_group_indicator = '-'`, guaranteeing only the four closed 0‑19 groups are counted and that the all‑ages (or 0 +) rows are excluded.  
• The join is on `country_code` only, so each country appears exactly once; the result shown matches the expected top‑10 list.

The other two versions either work but scan a much larger table (0result) or omit the `age_group_indicator` filter (2result), which could accidentally include an open‑ended age band in future data.  

```plaintext
1result.sql
```